            "description": "notification-service console (user.registered consumer) prints, per new account:\nNOTIFICATION [EMAIL -> <email>]: Welcome ... Activate your account: <link>\nFor the doctor and nurse:\n1. Set doctorPassword and nursePassword in this environment to a password (>= 8 chars).\n2. Open the link in a browser, enter that password twice, submit -> 'Your account is active'.\nIf the nurse got a resend (folder 01), use the NEWEST link ('activation link has been renewed').\nLinks expire after 1h (30m for a resend); re-run the resend request for a fresh one.\nDB check:\ndocker exec -it careround-postgres psql -U postgres -d careround_notification_db -c \"SELECT idempotency_key, channel, recipient, event_type, status, sent_at FROM sent_notifications ORDER BY sent_at DESC LIMIT 5;\"\npm.test('Passwords set in the environment for the next logins', function () {\npm.expect(pm.environment.get('doctorPassword'), 'doctorPassword').to.be.a('string').and.not.empty; pm.expect(pm.environment.get('nursePassword'), 'nursePassword').to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;\n});"
          },
